        "text": "Cefi still dominates many aspects of the crypto world. As of 2021, over 90% of crypto trading volume took place on centralized exchanges. DeFi, on the other hand, doesn't involve any middleman. Decentralized exchanges complete trades via self executing smart contracts and peer to peer transactions. Users interact with their own personal wallets and don't have to deposit crypto with a third party. Both DeFi and CEFI have their advantages and limitations. CEFI provides convenience and reduces the technical complications of managing various DEFI products on your own. Cefi also offers fiat to crypto trading services, and major platforms provide customer support. While DEFI gives users complete control over their crypto, more privacy, and many other attractive features, it has its limitations.",
